{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Many.</b> He returns to mention the words of those who seek falsehood, for when I was in distress, I and my men [were] saying, [those who] seek falsehood [were] upon me and upon my men." "<b>Who will show us good.</b> Some say: the word נסה is among the verbs with hidden lamed, [like] נס, and it ought to be on the pattern of וראה and עשה and בא, and it comes [as it is] in the way that it is, like: ואשעה בחוקיך. And it is correct that the heh is like the alef and the samekh is like the shin. There are verbs that are called hidden ayin, such as all the two-letter verbs, such as: קם שב, and they are all as if one says: קום שוב, for the middle letter is hidden, which corresponds to the ayin of the verb. And it is correct that the heh is like the alef and the samekh is like the shin, after the manner of: ישא ה' פניו אליך, and like: הנסה דבר אליך תלאה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "The phrase והם כלם כמו שיאמר קום שוב appears to mean 'they are all as if one says קום שוב' (i.e., as if the middle letter were quiescent); rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:25.330764731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}